menu "MEIT motor self-test"

config MEIT_MOTOR_TEST_INTENSITY_PCT
    int "Motor test intensity (%)"
    range 1 100
    default 15
    help
        Percent of MOTOR_DUTY_CAP (config.h), not of full duty. 100 means
        "average voltage = MOTOR_RATED_MV", which is only true once
        MOTOR_SUPPLY_MV matches the real motor rail. At the default 15 an
        ERM motor will very likely NOT start (a false "motor dead" result).
        Before increasing this value, first confirm the battery pack voltage
        and motor rating, then set MOTOR_SUPPLY_MV accordingly. Keep the first
        hardware check conservative and test one motor at a time.

config MEIT_MOTOR_TEST_ON_MS
    int "Time each motor stays on (ms)"
    range 100 5000
    default 700

config MEIT_MOTOR_TEST_GAP_MS
    int "Off time between motors (ms)"
    range 100 5000
    default 500

endmenu
